Clause 85
Termination for non-compliance with obligations
One. The Chief Executive may terminate the concession for the operation of games of fortune or chance in casinos, by unilateral
termination, in the event of non-compliance with obligations arising from legislation or from this concession contract to which the
Concessionaire is bound.
Two. The following, in particular, constitute grounds for unilateral termination of this concession contract:
1) The deviation of the scope of the concession, either through unauthorized gaming operation, or through the exercise of
activities excluded from the corporate scope of the Concessionaire;
2) The abandonment of the concession operation or its unjustified suspension for a period exceeding 7 consecutive days or 14
interspersed days in a calendar year;
3) The total or partial, temporary or definitive, transfer of the right of operation in non-compliance with the provisions of the
concession regime referred to in clause six;
4) Failure to pay the taxes, premiums, contributions, or other remuneration due to the Macau SAR provided for in the
